meta {
  name: 14. Cleanup - Delete Pipeline (safety net)
  type: http
  seq: 22
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:dataSetId/pipelines/:id
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  dataSetId: {{sqlDataSetId}}
  id: {{sqlPipelineId}}
}

tests {
  test("Pipeline already gone or deleted", function() {
    const status = res.getStatus();
    // After the DELETE saga (steps 12/13) the pipeline is already cascade-removed → 404.
    // 204 only occurs as a safety net for a never-provisioned / partially built run.
    expect(status === 204 || status === 404).to.be.true;
  });
}

docs {
  **SQL saga step 14** — Delete the pipeline (safety net).

  With the new delete contract this step is normally a no-op: the DATASET_DELETE saga (steps 12/13) already undeployed the NiFi flow and removed the pipeline via cascade, so this usually returns `404`. It remains only as a safety net for a run that never reached provisioning (e.g. a partially built dataset), where the pipeline record may still exist and returns `204`.

  **Expected Response:** 404 Not Found (already removed by the DELETE saga). 204 only for a never-provisioned run.
}
